completed_at: "2026-11-26T17:43:28.553Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 300
acceptance_criteria: "Windows recovery-text tests derive their expectations from the dialect renderer instead of a POSIX literal; The rendered-command safety test passes under bash 3.2 with history expansion, including non-ASCII arguments; A dispatched Nightly Validation run is green on every leg"
parent: pm-doxj
risk: high
confidence: 85
severity: high
resolution: "quotePosixCommandArg single-quotes an argument holding !, CR or LF, or ending in a backslash, the spellings bash 3.2's history pre-scan misreads in double quotes; the Windows recovery-text specs derive their expectations from the dialect renderer"
expected_result: "Every nightly leg passes: Windows tests compare recovery text through the dialect renderer, and a rendered POSIX command survives bash 3.2 with history expansion byte for byte"
actual_result: "33 hostile arguments round-trip byte for byte under bash 3.2; the three Windows specs pass under PM_COMMAND_SHELL=posix, cmd and powershell; dispatched Nightly Validation run 45851305902 is green on every leg"
